| Rank | Target | KNOWN rigorous benchmark | Result of this investigation | Main remaining obligation | Success probability* |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| **1** | Recursive factoring | \(L_N[1/2,1]\), Lenstra–Pomerance 1992 | **PROVED from A:** fixed point \(C_\theta=\sqrt{(1+\sqrt2)\theta}\); consequently every positive \(L[1/2]\) constant | Write the recursive expected-time argument with slack | **95%**; major |
| **2** | Discrete logarithms in \(\mathbb F_p^\times\) | \(L_p[1/2,\sqrt2]\), Pomerance 1987 | **PROVED reduction from A’s supply lemmas:** every positive \(L[1/2]\) constant, using exact multiplicative dependencies | Audit the prime-input transfer and the certificate implementation | **85%**; major |
| **3** | \(\varphi(N)\), \(\lambda(N)\), multiplicative orders | \(L_N[1/2,1]\), through factoring | **PROVED from A:** inherit the factoring bound, including the recursive improvement | None mathematically | **>99%**; useful corollaries |
| **4** | Factoring with a fixed exponent \(\alpha<1/2\) | \(L_N[1/2,1]\) | **SPECULATIVE:** \(L[3/7,O(1)]\) is a plausible conservative target; \(L[2/5,O(1)]\) needs stronger uniformity | Quantitative FM/LD* as \(d,k\) grow | **40%** for some \(\alpha<1/2\); **20%** for \(2/5\) |
| **5** | Extension-field DL in intermediate characteristic | Bender–Pomerance’s \(L[1/2,\sqrt2]\) in its range; Kleinjung–Wesolowski elsewhere | **SPECULATIVE:** function-field version of the construction could improve the \(L[1/2]\) constant | Polynomial-ring FM/LD*, geometricity, and constant-field bookkeeping | **35%**; potentially major |
